# Module Separation of Concerns - Development Rule

## Purpose
Enforce strict separation of responsibilities across module layers to ensure maintainable, testable, and scalable React applications. Each layer has ONE clear responsibility and follows the single responsibility principle rigorously.

## Architecture Principles

### The Golden Rule
**"Components render. Hooks orchestrate. Services fetch. Utils transform. Types define. Constants declare."**

Each file should answer to exactly ONE of these verbs. If a file does multiple things, it should be split.

### File Size Constraints
- **Components**: < 250 lines (ideally < 150)
- **Pages**: < 300 lines (ideally < 200)
- **Hooks**: < 200 lines (ideally < 150)
- **Services**: < 150 lines per domain
- **Utils**: < 100 lines per file
- **Types**: No limit (but organize by domain)
- **Constants**: < 100 lines per file

## Layer Responsibilities

### 1. Components Layer (`components/{Module}/`)

**SOLE RESPONSIBILITY**: Presentation and rendering logic ONLY

#### ✅ ALLOWED
```tsx
// components/Transaction/TransactionCard.tsx
interface TransactionCardProps {
  transaction: Transaction
  onClick?: (id: string) => void
  onEdit?: (id: string) => void
}

export default function TransactionCard({ transaction, onClick, onEdit }: TransactionCardProps) {
  const { id, amount, date, type, status } = transaction
  
  return (
    <div className="border rounded-lg p-4" onClick={() => onClick?.(id)}>
      <div className="flex justify-between items-center">
        <span className="font-semibold">{formatCurrency(amount)}</span>
        <StatusBadge status={status} />
      </div>
      <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">{formatDate(date)}</p>
      {onEdit && (
        <button onClick={(e) => {
          e.stopPropagation()
          onEdit(id)
        }}>
          Edit
        </button>
      )}
    </div>
  )
}
```

**RULES**:
- ✅ Receive data via props
- ✅ Call callbacks for user interactions
- ✅ Use utility functions for formatting (imported)
- ✅ Conditional rendering based on props
- ✅ useContext ONLY for theme/i18n
- ❌ NO useState (except for pure UI state like hover, expanded)
- ❌ NO useEffect (except for DOM manipulation)
- ❌ NO API calls
- ❌ NO business logic
- ❌ NO data transformations
- ❌ NO complex calculations

#### ❌ FORBIDDEN ANTI-PATTERN
```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Component doing too much
export default function TransactionCard({ transactionId }: { transactionId: string }) {
  const [transaction, setTransaction] = useState(null)
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)
  
  useEffect(() => {
    // ❌ NO: API call in component
    fetchTransaction(transactionId).then(setTransaction)
  }, [transactionId])
  
  // ❌ NO: Business logic in component
  const total = transaction.items.reduce((sum, item) => {
    return sum + (item.quantity * item.price * (1 + item.taxRate))
  }, 0)
  
  return <div>{total}</div>
}
```

