### 2. Pages Layer (`pages/{Module}/`)

**SOLE RESPONSIBILITY**: Route orchestration and composition

#### ✅ ALLOWED
```tsx
// pages/Transaction/TransactionListPage.tsx
export default function TransactionListPage() {
  const navigate = useNavigate()
  const { hasPermission } = usePermissions()
  
  // ALL logic comes from hooks
  const {
    transactions,
    isLoading,
    error,
    filters,
    handleFilterChange,
    handleSort,
    stats
  } = useTransactionList()
  
  const { deleteTransaction, isDeleting } = useTransactionActions()
  
  // Simple handlers that delegate
  const handleTransactionClick = (id: string) => navigate(`/transactions/${id}`)
  const handleCreate = () => navigate('/transactions/create')
  const handleDelete = async (id: string) => {
    if (confirm('Delete this transaction?')) {
      await deleteTransaction(id)
    }
  }
  
  // UI state management
  if (isLoading) return <Loader />
  if (error) return <ErrorState error={error} onRetry={refetch} />
  if (transactions.length === 0) return <EmptyState onCreateClick={handleCreate} />
  
  return (
    <div className="p-6">
      <PageHeader 
        title="Transactions" 
        subtitle={`${stats.total} transactions`}
        action={hasPermission('transaction:create') && (
          <Button onClick={handleCreate}>Create Transaction</Button>
        )}
      />
      
      <TransactionFilters 
        filters={filters} 
        onChange={handleFilterChange} 
      />
      
      <TransactionList 
        transactions={transactions}
        onClick={handleTransactionClick}
        onDelete={hasPermission('transaction:delete') ? handleDelete : undefined}
        isDeleting={isDeleting}
      />
    </div>
  )
}
```

**RULES**:
- ✅ Import and use custom hooks
- ✅ Compose presentation components
- ✅ Handle routing (navigate, params)
- ✅ Handle permissions
- ✅ Simple UI state (modals open/close)
- ✅ Delegate to callbacks
- ❌ NO business logic
- ❌ NO direct API calls
- ❌ NO data transformations
- ❌ NO complex state management
- ❌ NO useMemo/useCallback (leave that to hooks)

